        "note": [
          "Statistics on deaths within 30 days of a fire due to burns or smoke inhalation, as assessed by the Swedish Civil Defence and Resilience Agency on the basis of information from the municipal fire and rescue service, the police, the Swedish Transport Administration, the National Forensic Centre (1999-2015) and the national burns centres in Linköping and Uppsala.\r\n\r\nIn these statistics, a residential building is understood to be either a block of flats, a detached house, a terraced or semi-detached house or a summer house. Institutional forms of accommodation such as sheltered housing, care homes, nursing homes, communal housing and student residences are not included in this category.\r\n\r\n'Day of Week' and 'Time of Fire' are estimates of when the fire started.\r\n\r\n"
